  "instructions": [
    "Combine the rice, water, and 1/2 tsp salt in a medium pot. Bring to a boil, cover, and reduce the heat to low. Cook 15 minutes, then rest off the heat, covered, until the water is absorbed.",
    "Toss the chicken with 1 tsp salt. Heat the oil in a 12 inch skillet over medium-high heat.",
    "Add the chicken in one layer and cook 4 minutes, stirring once, until lightly browned. Move it to a plate. It will not be cooked through yet.",
    "Lower the heat to medium. Add the onion to the same skillet and cook 4 minutes until soft.",
    "Stir in the garlic, ginger, garam masala, cumin, and paprika. Cook 1 minute until fragrant.",
    "Pour in the tomato sauce and scrape up any browned bits. Simmer 3 minutes.",
    "Return the chicken and its juices to the skillet. Simmer 6 minutes until the chicken reaches 165 F.",
    "Stir in the cream and heat 2 minutes without boiling hard. Fluff the rice and serve the chicken and sauce over it.",
    "For leftovers, cool within 2 hours and store the chicken and rice in airtight containers. Freeze up to 3 months, and reheat until steaming hot."
  ],
